<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ shop.locale | default: 'en' }}">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>{{ page_title | default: shop.name }}</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ 'theme.css' | asset_url }}">
  {% comment %}
    Without this, settings.heading_font/body_font below were only ever a
    CSS `font-family` declaration with nothing to back it — the browser
    has no way to fetch "Poppins"/"Outfit"/whatever a merchant typed
    unless the actual @font-face is loaded, so every page silently fell
    back to the generic system sans-serif regardless of what Theme
    Settings said. Both settings default to the same font (Outfit) in a
    fresh install, so this normally requests it once; Google Fonts
    tolerates a repeated `family=` param fine on the rare theme that sets
    them differently.
  {% endcomment %}
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link
    rel="stylesheet"
    href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family={{ settings.heading_font | default: 'Outfit' | replace: ' ', '+' }}:wght@400;500;600;700&family={{ settings.body_font | default: 'Outfit' | replace: ' ', '+' }}:wght@400;500;600&display=swap"
  >
  {% comment %}
    theme.css's :root block is just static fallback values — these
    settings-driven custom properties come after it in the cascade, so
    they win. This is what makes the Theme Settings drawer (colors,
    fonts, layout) actually affect the rendered storefront instead of
    only updating a database row nothing reads.
  {% endcomment %}
  <style>
    :root {
      --color-primary: {{ settings.color_primary | default: '#111111' }};
      --color-accent: {{ settings.color_accent | default: '#FE8138' }};
      --color-background: {{ settings.color_background | default: '#FFF8EE' }};
      --color-text: {{ settings.color_text | default: '#1A1613' }};
      --container-width: {{ settings.container_width | default: 1360 }}px;
      --button-radius: {{ settings.button_radius | default: 999 }}px;
    }
    body { font-family: '{{ settings.body_font | default: "Outfit" }}', sans-serif; }
    h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6 { font-family: '{{ settings.heading_font | default: "Outfit" }}', sans-serif; }
  </style>
  {% render 'snippets/installed-apps' %}
</head>
<body>
  {% section 'announcement-bar' %}
  {% section 'header' %}

  <main>
    {{ content_for_layout }}
  </main>

  {% section 'footer' %}
  <script src="{{ 'theme.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
</body>
</html>
